    "public_preview": null,
    "text": "Let’s be clear: Pride was never just about rainbows, parades, or corporate logos. It has always been about people. It has always been about protecting the right of every person to exist safely, openly, and freely.\n\nAt a time when LGBTQIA+ people, especially trans people, are facing increasing attacks on their rights, healthcare, visibility, and dignity, Pride remains as necessary as ever. Not because progress hasn’t been made, but because progress is fragile.\n\nThe rights we celebrate today are the result of people who organized, protested, resisted, and refused to disappear. And our responsibility is to ensure the next generation inherits more freedom, not less.\n\nThis page was built by a Black queer kid from the South who was once told people like him shouldn’t exist. The words you read here, the community built here, and the life lessons shared here are shaped by that lived experience.\n\nSo Happy Pride Month to everyone who has also experienced being told they were too much, not enough, or unworthy of belonging. You’ll always have a home here in this community. \n\nYou deserve to be here. You always have. 🫶🏽 \n\n✨ Featured artist to follow (slides 1-6): @sterlinggraves ✨\n\nwe the urban words: @williegreene_\n\n#pride #pridemonth",
    "word_count": 205
  },
